  "description": "We have defined two distinct hierarchies for our system. The first hierarchy, **Employee**, lives under the namespace\u202f`company.hr.employee` and is not treated as a postfix element. Its primary identifier is the `employeeId` field. Within this hierarchy we have a sub\u2011type called **Manager**, which inherits from\u202fEmployee and adds a `department` attribute to capture the manager\u2019s business unit.\n\nThe second hierarchy, **Product**, is scoped to `inventory.product` and is configured to be used as a postfix. The core property for this hierarchy is `sku`, the stock\u2011keeping unit that uniquely identifies each product. A specialized sub\u2011type named **DigitalProduct** is also defined; it does not inherit from any other type (its super\u2011type is\u202fnull) and introduces a `downloadUrl` property to store the location where the digital item can be retrieved.",
  "reference_json": {
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema",
    "hierarchies": [
      {
        "name": "Employee",
        "path": "company.hr.employee",
        "asPostfix": false,
        "baseProperties": {
          "name": "employeeId"
        },
        "subTypes": {
          "name": "Manager",
          "superType": "Employee",
          "properties": {
            "name": "department"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "Product",
        "path": "inventory.product",
        "asPostfix": true,
        "baseProperties": {
          "name": "sku"
        },
        "subTypes": {
          "name": "DigitalProduct",
          "superType": null,
          "properties": {
            "name": "downloadUrl"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
